## 4. CONTROLLABLE ANNOUNCEMENT POPUP SYSTEM

Build a complete popup and promotional announcement management system connected to the admin dashboard.

This is a mandatory feature.

### Popup functionality

The admin must be able to:
- Enable or disable the popup instantly.
- Create multiple popup campaigns.
- Select which popup is currently active.
- Edit the popup headline, description, button text, button link, image, and background.
- Change text color, background color, and button style.
- Upload or replace popup images.
- Select popup layouts, including centered modal, image-and-text layout, and compact announcement popup.
- Choose between promotional, welcome, coupon, newsletter, and general announcement popups.
- Schedule a start date and end date.
- Set the popup to appear immediately or after a configurable delay.
- Choose whether the popup appears on the homepage, product pages, collection pages, or selected pages.
- Select desktop, mobile, or all devices.
- Set display frequency, such as once per session, once per day, or once per visitor within a defined period.
- Configure a close button and ensure visitors can dismiss it.
- Set a cooldown period before the popup appears again.
- Preview the popup before publishing.
- Save campaigns as drafts.
- Publish, pause, archive, or delete campaigns.
- View basic impressions, clicks, and conversion metrics where measurable.

### Example welcome popup

Headline: "A Little Love Awaits You"

Description: "Discover sweet newborn essentials made for life's most precious moments."

Button: "Explore the Collection"

Optional coupon example: "Use LITTLE10 for 10% off selected products."

Only activate the coupon example when the matching discount exists in the database.

### Popup behavior

- Never display the popup on every page load if the configured frequency prevents it.
- Never repeatedly reopen the popup after a visitor closes it during the configured suppression period.
- Prevent multiple popups from appearing simultaneously.
- Do not block checkout or essential navigation.
- Ensure the popup works on mobile devices and is accessible using a keyboard.
- Do not require newsletter signup to close a promotional popup.
- Collect email addresses only with appropriate consent and a valid privacy notice.
- Do not display expired or unpublished campaigns.
- Apply scheduled campaign changes automatically.
- Store popup settings in the database so the admin can update them without redeploying the website.

### Announcement bar management

Create a separate admin section for announcement bars.

Allow the admin to:
- Create multiple announcement messages.
- Select the active message.
- Enable or disable the bar.
- Configure text, background, text color, and optional link.
- Schedule publication and expiry.
- Display a single message or rotate through multiple messages.
- Set rotation intervals where rotation is enabled.
- Preview changes before publishing.

The announcement bar and popup must be independently configurable.

