## 19. FINAL DELIVERY REQUIREMENTS

Build the actual connected application, including the frontend, backend, database, secure admin dashboard, product management, discounts, inventory, configurable payment methods, announcement management, popup campaigns, order management, email automation, and supplier fulfillment workflows.

Do not stop after generating a homepage or visual mockup.

Implement the database and backend first, then connect the admin dashboard and customer storefront to the same persistent data.

If an external integration requires merchant approval, API credentials, or additional configuration, build the appropriate integration interface and clearly document the remaining setup steps.

Never pretend that payments, emails, supplier synchronization, or automated fulfillment work until they have been configured and tested.

The finished store should be elegant, secure, manageable without coding, and suitable for a real newborn clothing dropshipping business targeting customers in Pakistan, with the flexibility to expand internationally later.